 "about": "T1.32g part 2c's vectors, written by the independent test author: a map's and a union's canonical cells, which run_python's arrow_values and sdm-testkit's values must both give. A map is [\"map\", [[key, value], ...]], its entries in the order Arrow holds them (duplicates kept), a null map null, an empty one [\"map\", []]. A union is [\"union\", type code, member name, the member's cell], never null itself: a null member, or a union DuckDB writes as null (a null under its first member), is the member's tag with a null cell. A vector with 'sql' runs on DuckDB; one with 'build' is built as Arrow by each test (DuckDB writes no duplicate map key and no dense union). A value of a type the form does not hold stays [\"?\", \"arrow:<type>\"] and is listed unencodable, inside a map or a chosen member too; a member not chosen names nothing. An interval is [\"interval\", months, days, nanoseconds] since part 2e (contract/t132g-p2e-vectors.json).",
